5. TITLE BAR COLOR PICKER REQUIRED USER GESTURE (2026-06-26)
   Status: Fixed in current build
   Symptom: View > Title Bar Color... logged "A user gesture is required to show the color picker" and did not open a picker.

   Root cause:
   - The Electron menu click sent an IPC event to the renderer.
   - The renderer then tried to open a hidden `<input type="color">`.
   - Chromium does not treat a delayed IPC callback as the original user gesture, so it blocked the picker.

   Fix:
   - View > Title Bar Color... now opens a native Windows color dialog from the Electron main process.
   - The selected color is normalized to `#RRGGBB`, applied to the native title bar, and saved to `qmail-window-settings.json`.
   - Reset Title Bar Color remains disabled when the current color is the default Pear color (`#C9CC3F`) and becomes active after a custom color is selected.

   Test:
   - Launch QMail.exe and confirm the title bar defaults to Pear unless a saved custom titleBarColor exists.
   - Select View > Title Bar Color..., choose a color, and confirm the title bar changes with no console user-gesture error.
   - Restart QMail.exe and confirm the custom color persists.
   - Select View > Reset Title Bar Color and confirm the title bar returns to Pear.

